  _1980 Mathematics Subject Classification._ Primary 05-02, 05A05, 05A10, 05A15,
  05A19, 32A25; Secondary 05A17, 05B20, 05B35, 05C05, 05C15, 05C30, 05C45,
  13F25, 20D10, 20F14, 20F16, 20F19, 30C40, 32A05, 32A27, 32C25, 32C30, 32C37,
  32H10, 33A35, 40B05, 40C05, 40E05, 41A60, 82A99.

  *Abstract.* This book contains investigations on the problem of finding
  integral representations for and computing finite and infinite sums
  (generating functions) arising in practice in combinatorial analysis, the
  theory of algorithms and programming on a computer, probability theory, group
  theory, function theory, and so on, as well as in physics and other areas of
  knowledge. A general approach is presented for computing sums (expressions) in
  closed form by reducing them to one-dimensional and multiple integrals, most
  often contour integrals. The monograph may be useful to specialists in
  discrete and continuous mathematics, physicists, engineers, and others
  interested in computing sums and applying complex analysis in discrete
  mathematics.
]
